{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-480f4aa276ea", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:41:01.900Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 0, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:41:08.797Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 13372, "tokens_out": 102, "latency": 6.872, "finish_reason": "tool_use"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "What does our reserving guidance say about setting an initial reserve on a new claim?", "prompt_hash": "sha256:35c2f9ad3629a832d68ffc1f7ce464ce9630699fd7862ccbfeb01bf1c01bb4d7", "response_text": "I'll search our reserving guidance for information about setting initial reserves on new claims.", "response_hash": "sha256:405b0de5374884b15aae608f073566c0816b5f5a1729cb8683d24316de4b877e", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-480f4aa276ea", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:41:01.900Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 1, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:41:09.057Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 14538, "tokens_out": 235, "latency": 0.2592, "finish_reason": "end_turn"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "What does our reserving guidance say about setting an initial reserve on a new claim?", "prompt_hash": "sha256:35c2f9ad3629a832d68ffc1f7ce464ce9630699fd7862ccbfeb01bf1c01bb4d7", "response_text": "Our reserving guidance (prc-reserving-001) says:\n\n**Set an opening reserve within one working day of the claim being notified.**\n\nWhere information is limited, use the class average from the table rather than leaving the reserve at nil. A nil reserve on an open claim is treated as a reporting error, not a neutral position.\n\nThe class averages are:\n- Motor, own damage: £2,400\n- Motor, third party property: £3,100\n- Motor, third party injury: £12,000\n- Household, escape of water: £4,800\n- Household, subsidence: £18,000\n- Commercial property: £9,500\n- Professional indemnity: £25,000\n\nThe guidance also notes that you should record the reason for each reserve movement in the claim note, and that reserves move on a review timetable based on claim size (every 90 days under £10,000; every 60 days for £10,000–£100,000; every 30 days above £100,000).", "response_hash": "sha256:d00a82206cbcc20313624b129cffcee1ab0222a14afa9f60b7ab3cbedeee6cd4", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
